# ⚠️ AND ITS SEED, WHICH MUST TRAVEL WITH IT (2026-09-02). `prisma/seed-e2e.ts`
# does `import { E2E } from '../e2e/accounts'`, so ignoring the folder while
# uploading the importer sent Railway a file whose module does not exist —
# `tsconfig` includes `**/*.ts` and `next build` type-checks it. Every deploy
# after the seed was written (2026-09-02 10:56) failed with:
#
#     Type error: Cannot find module '../e2e/accounts'
#
# ⚠️ `npm run check` CANNOT CATCH THIS AND NEVER WILL. Its `next build` runs
# against the working tree, where `e2e/` is present — the gate is green and the
# deploy is broken, because the two do not see the same set of files. That is
# the hazard `railway up` carries by design (CLAUDE.md: „uploads the WORKING
# TREE"), and the only defence is that anything ignored here is ignored WITH
# whatever imports it.
#
# It is dev tooling by the same argument as the line above: its own header says
# it refuses to run against anything but a local database, and `npm run e2e:seed`
# is the only caller.
prisma/seed-e2e.ts
